Now CSS. Add to `.card-glyph` section and `.portrait`. Need consider `.avatar-portrait` class base. Add after `.card-glyph .icon` rules.

Also `.card-glyph.avatar` shouldn't have `filter`? Keep drop-shadow on container could apply to image, fine. But glyph has place-items center; okay. `.glyph-portrait` absolute? Let container `position:relative; display:block;`. Width 54px from parent.

CSS:
```
.card-glyph.avatar { position:relative; color:var(--c); filter:none; }
.card-glyph.avatar .glyph-portrait { display:block; width:100%; height:100%; border-radius:50%; overflow:hidden; border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--c) 60%, transparent); background: radial-gradient(circle at 50% 30%, var(--cs), rgba(7,10,20,.9) 75%); box-shadow: 0 0 18px -6px var(--c), inset 0 0 12px -6px var(--c); }
.card-glyph.avatar .avatar-portrait { width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; transform:scale(1.22); transform-origin:50% 32%; }
.glyph-element { position:absolute; right:-5px; bottom:-3px; width:20px; height:20px; border-radius:50%; background:#090b16; border:1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--c) 75%, transparent); display:grid; place-items:center; color:var(--c); box-shadow:0 0 10px -2px var(--c); }
.glyph-element .icon { width:12px;height:12px;filter:none; }
```
But `.card-glyph .icon` has `filter: drop-shadow`, override.

HUD:
```
.portrait { overflow:hidden; }
.portrait .avatar-portrait { width:100%; height:100%; object-fit:cover; transform:scale(1.28); transform-origin:50% 30%; }
```
Need ensure portrait image is circular: parent has border-radius 50 + overflow hidden.
But the portrait has transparent background; HUD portrait background radial already. Good.

Potential issue: the image is 1024x1024, and if object-fit cover + scale 1.22, the head fills circle. With transform-origin 50% 32%, the face may shift. We can test.

Let's add CSS.

